   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = 2 x + y \\) with \\( f(3) = -1 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(2) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 3 \\) with two steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         -17,
         4
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{2 - (3)}{2} = - \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (3, -1) \\) the slope is \\( 5 \\), so \\( y \\approx -1 + (- \\frac{1}{2})(5) = - \\frac{7}{2} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{5}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -7,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{5}{2}, - \\frac{7}{2}) \\) the slope is \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\), so \\( y \\approx - \\frac{7}{2} + (- \\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{3}{2}) = - \\frac{17}{4} \\) at \\( x = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -17,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( f(2) \\approx - \\frac{17}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -17,
            4
         ]
      }
